From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Install the import library

install(TARGETS) names RUNTIME and LIBRARY but not ARCHIVE. On ELF there is
no import library and the omission costs nothing. On Windows ARCHIVE is the
import library -- the half a consumer actually links against -- so without
it the installed alpm_octopi_utils_target.cmake has no IMPORTED_IMPLIB, and
find_package(alpm_octopi_utils) fails at generate time in any project that
uses it. octopi is one.

Worth sending upstream.
diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 8bb65a8..72bf247 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -31,7 +31,11 @@ if(WIN32)
   target_include_directories(alpm_octopi_utils PRIVATE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/win32")
 endif()
 target_link_libraries(alpm_octopi_utils PUBLIC glib-2.0::glib-2.0 PUBLIC gobject-2.0::gobject-2.0 PUBLIC gio-2.0::gio-2.0 PUBLIC alpm::alpm)
-install(TARGETS alpm_octopi_utils EXPORT alpm_octopi_utils_target RUNTIME DESTINATION bin LIBRARY DESTINATION lib PUBLIC_HEADER DESTINATION include)
+# ARCHIVE is the import library. On ELF there is none and the omission costs
+# nothing; on Windows it is the half a consumer links against, and without
+# it the exported target has no IMPORTED_IMPLIB, so every find_package() of
+# this library fails at generate time rather than at link time.
+install(TARGETS alpm_octopi_utils EXPORT alpm_octopi_utils_target RUNTIME DESTINATION bin LIBRARY DESTINATION lib ARCHIVE DESTINATION lib PUBLIC_HEADER DESTINATION include)
 install(EXPORT alpm_octopi_utils_target DESTINATION lib/cmake/alpm_octopi_utils)
 install(FILES "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/alpm_octopi_utils.h" DESTINATION include)
 install(FILES "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/alpm_octopi_utils.vapi" DESTINATION share/vala/vapi)
